  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "package-root-import",
      "lines": [
        "1 package is imported by their root in src, so the whole barrel is reachable and the bundler keeps whatever it cannot prove unused:",
        "  @nextcloud/vue: 15,851 B in 23 modules, 1.3 % of the static path of checksum-main.mjs, imported by its root in views/ChecksumTab.vue (NcButton, NcLoadingIcon, NcSelect, ...).",
        "Importing the module that is used instead of the package root lets the bundler drop the rest of the barrel.",
        "ncmake's lint-vue-imports workflow gates exactly this specifier for @nextcloud/vue, so this finding is that red check with a byte figure attached."
      ],
      "covers": [
        "bundle-report/package-root-imported",
        "lint-vue-imports"
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "unreferenced-components",
      "lines": [
        "15 components of @nextcloud/vue are delivered although no file in src names them, no other dependency names them and no component named by either imports them: 7,619 B, 0.6 % of the static path of checksum-main.mjs, next to 1 component the source names and 1 those pull in.",
        "  NcRichText 5,027 B, NcPopover 1,336 B, NcEmojiPicker 559 B, NcProgressBar 300 B, NcRelatedResourcesPanel 152 B, NcSettingsSelectGroup 94 B, and 9 more.",
        "These arrive through the root import: under a barrel the whole component set is reachable, so the bundler must keep it. Per-component imports leave it free to drop what the app never names."
      ]
    },
